--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repo targets Swift 6.0 on a pinned toolchain; the available runner is the NEWER
Xcode 26.5 (Swift 6.x), whose stricter front-end rejects two PRE-EXISTING, out-of-scope
files that are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via `git status`) and outside this
artifact's allowed files. They fail identically on a clean tree (the repo's macOS
verification is documented PENDING in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md):

  1) apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift
     10x "cannot use explicit 'return' statement in the body of result builder 'ViewBuilder'"
     — all inside `#if DEBUG` #Preview blocks of the Input field component.
  2) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift:20
     "call to main actor-isolated static method ... in a synchronous nonisolated context"

To exercise build+test for THIS page without editing out-of-scope files, both were
isolated via the command-line build setting
  EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES='Input.Previews.swift GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift'
(a build override, no source edits). With them isolated the app target builds clean and
this page's 24 tests pass (above). No SleepEfficiency / AppRoute / TeslaSyncApp file
produced any diagnostic. The literal unmodified `xcodebuild build test` is therefore
blocked SOLELY by these pre-existing, unrelated toolchain-compat files — not by this
page. Fixing them would breach this artifact's allowed-files scope, so they are left
untouched.

